  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 152706765a7dec6419e3ec12554375ac, type: 3}
  m_Name: BusinessModelCourse
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  courseName: Business Model Course
  courseDescription: Choose the best-fit business model for your goals, lifestyle, skills, and experience.
  accentColor: {r: 0.13, g: 0.55, b: 0.88, a: 1}
  lessons:
  - title: Start Here
    description: Jake introduces a framework to help you choose the best-fit business
      model for your goals, lifestyle, skills, and experience. This chapter explains
      that every person has a different ideal business and helps you think through
      how involved you want to be before choosing your path.
    videoUrl: https://player.vimeo.com/video/1075842787
    thumbnail: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Understanding Business Archetypes
    description: This chapter explains the three core business archetypes&#58; Done-For-You,
      Do-It-Yourself, and Done-With-You. You will learn how each model works, how
      hands-on each one is, and how to choose the right service layer based on your
      skillset, goals, and preferred level of involvement.
    videoUrl: https://player.vimeo.com/video/1075842883
    thumbnail: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Proximity to Proof
    description: This chapter helps you pick the right industry and skill combination
      by using your existing credibility. It covers personal experience, helping friends
      or family, behind-the-scenes access, formal education, and shared identity or
      community as ways to build trust faster.
    videoUrl: https://player.vimeo.com/video/1075843010
    thumbnail: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Choosing the Right Client/Customer Model
    description: This chapter explains the difference between clients and customers.
      Customers usually buy lower-ticket self-serve products, while clients usually
      buy higher-ticket support, consulting, or services. You will learn how to choose
      between volume, depth, or a hybrid value ladder.
    videoUrl: https://player.vimeo.com/video/1075842568
    thumbnail: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Offer & Model Matching
    description: This chapter shows how to match your offer to the right delivery
      model. It explains DIY offers like courses and tools, DWY offers like coaching
      and consulting, and DFY offers like services or agencies. The goal is to start
      with one clear offer and productize it before scaling.
    videoUrl: https://player.vimeo.com/video/1075842602
    thumbnail: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Monetization Frameworks
    description: This chapter explains three ways to monetize your business&#58; direct
      sales, value ladder, and trust building. Direct sales is usually fastest to
      cash. A value ladder builds long-term customer value. Trust building uses free
      content or lead magnets to nurture buyers over time.
    videoUrl: https://player.vimeo.com/video/1075842641
    thumbnail: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Picking Your Model - The Decision Flowchart
    description: This chapter gives you a step-by-step process for choosing the right
      business model. It helps you consider industry fit, involvement level, skillset,
      the problem you can solve, market economics, and income structure before locking
      in your model.
    videoUrl: https://player.vimeo.com/video/1075842692
    thumbnail: {fileID: 0}
  - title: Final Considerations & Resources
    description: This chapter covers final decisions before launch. It explains why
      you should differentiate your offer, avoid markets with no demand, avoid niches
      where buyers do not value the problem, and focus on testing, selling, and improving
      quickly instead of overbuilding.
    videoUrl: https://player.vimeo.com/video/1075842731
    thumbnail: {fileID: 0}
